---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import EmailLink from '@/components/EmailLink.astro';
import { buildMeta } from '@/utils/seo';
import { getSiteSettings } from '@/utils/reader';

const site = await getSiteSettings();

const meta = buildMeta({
  title: 'Cancellation Policy',
  description: 'Cancellation and rescheduling policy for Panun Kaergar bookings.',
  path: '/cancellation',
});
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">Cancellation Policy</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-slate mt-8 max-w-none">
    <p>
      Panun Kaergar is your point of contact for every booking. We manage customer acquisition,
      booking, pricing, communication, coordination, payment collection, support, and complaint
      handling. Independent service partners perform the work on site to our service standards, but
      your booking relationship is with Panun Kaergar.
    </p>
    <p>
      This page explains how to cancel or reschedule a booking, what happens when Panun Kaergar or a
      partner cancels, and how your payment is affected depending on whether a partner has visited
      the site and how much you have paid. Full refund rules — including quality, damage, and
      incomplete-service cases — are in our <a href="/refund">refund policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>1. How to cancel or reschedule</h2>
    <p>
      You can cancel or reschedule a booking through the Panun Kaergar customer app, or by contacting
      our team with your booking reference:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Open your booking in the Panun Kaergar customer app and choose cancel or reschedule, or</li>
      <li>
        Call us at <a href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>{site.phone}</a>, WhatsApp us, or email
        <EmailLink email={site.email} /> with your booking reference and preferred new time (if
        rescheduling)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Please cancel or reschedule as early as you can. Whether money is refunded after a cancellation
      depends on partner visit status and the rules below.
    </p>

    <h2>2. When you cancel the service</h2>
    <p>
      If you cancel a booked service, refund eligibility depends on whether our partner has already
      visited the site.
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has visited the site</h3>
    <p>
      If the service is cancelled by you after our partner has visited the site, the booking
      confirmation amount is not refundable. This amount covers the partner’s visit and related
      booking confirmation costs and will be retained.
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has not visited the site</h3>
    <p>
      If the service is cancelled by you and our partner has not visited the site, the amount paid
      for the booking will be refunded. You are eligible for a full refund of what you have paid
      toward that booking (subject to verification of payment and booking status).
    </p>

    <h2>3. When you have paid the full booking amount in advance</h2>
    <p>
      Sometimes customers pay the full booking amount in advance rather than only the booking
      confirmation amount. If you cancel in those cases, the following applies:
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has only visited</h3>
    <p>
      If you have paid the full booking amount in advance and the partner has only visited the site
      (for example, the visit happened and you then cancel, or the full service was not completed as
      booked), only the booking confirmation amount will be deducted. The remaining balance of the
      full amount you paid in advance will be refunded to you.
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has not visited</h3>
    <p>
      If you have paid the full booking amount in advance and the partner has not visited the site,
      the entire amount paid will be refunded. No booking confirmation deduction applies when the
      partner has not visited.
    </p>

    <h2>4. When Panun Kaergar cancels or reschedules</h2>
    <p>
      Panun Kaergar may cancel or reschedule a booking when a partner is unavailable, there is a
      partner no-show, operational constraints prevent the visit, or another genuine reason makes
      the scheduled service impossible. In such cases we will try to offer a suitable reschedule
      first.
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has not visited the site</h3>
    <p>
      If Panun Kaergar cancels the booking before a partner has visited, and you do not accept a
      suitable reschedule, amounts paid toward that booking will be refunded in full.
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has visited the site</h3>
    <p>
      If a partner has already visited and Panun Kaergar cancels the remainder of the service for
      reasons on our side, refund treatment will follow the applicable booking and payment rules
      described in our <a href="/refund">refund policy</a>, including any booking confirmation
      amount already earned for the visit.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Rescheduling</h2>
    <p>
      You may request a reschedule instead of a cancellation by using the app or contacting
      support with your booking reference and a preferred new time. Rescheduling is subject to
      partner availability. If a suitable new slot cannot be arranged and the booking is cancelled
      instead, the cancellation and refund rules above apply based on whether the partner has visited
      and who initiated the cancellation.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Payments and scope changes</h2>
    <p>
      Panun Kaergar sets and confirms the customer-facing price for each booking. Please pay only
      the amount approved by Panun Kaergar through our official booking and payment process. If
      additional work, changes in scope, or extra materials are needed on site, contact Panun
      Kaergar before any extra charge is agreed or collected. Do not cancel a booking to arrange
      service privately outside the platform.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You cancel + partner has visited → booking confirmation amount is not refundable.</li>
      <li>You cancel + partner has not visited → amount paid is refunded.</li>
      <li>
        Full amount paid in advance + partner has only visited → booking confirmation amount
        deducted; remaining amount refunded.
      </li>
      <li>Full amount paid in advance + partner has not visited → full amount refunded.</li>
      <li>
        Panun Kaergar cancels before a partner visit and no suitable reschedule → full refund of
        amounts paid.
      </li>
      <li>
        Quality, damage, incomplete work, duplicate charges, and refund processing → see our
        <a href="/refund">refund policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Related policies</h2>
    <p>
      For refunds related to poor workmanship, damage, incomplete service, duplicate charges, or
      processing timelines after an approved refund, see our
      <a href="/refund">refund policy</a>. For help with a specific booking,
      <a href="/contact">contact support</a> or see our <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
    </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
